# The skip ledger is append-only lines that are independent of each other, so a
# union merge is correct where a conflict carries no information (cleat#1333).
# Its one bad case -- two streams editing one line, which union duplicates --
# is caught by the duplicate check in scripts/check-skip-budget.sh rather than
# left to trust.
#
# THIS DOES NOT SOLVE THE PROBLEM ON GITHUB, and the comment here said it did
# until cleat#1395. Server-side mergeability does not consult .gitattributes,
# so a PR appending to this file still goes DIRTY the moment another one
# merges. Measured on one pair of heads, all three cases:
#
#     local merge, this file present     clean
#     local merge, this file removed     CONFLICT
#     GitHub, the same two heads         CONFLICTING / DIRTY
#
# The line below is kept because it genuinely helps every `git merge` and
# `git rebase` a human runs. The actual fix is scripts/skip-ledger.d/ -- one
# file per declaration, so two streams have nothing to conflict over anywhere.
# New declarations go there; see its README.
#
# Deliberately NOT applied to IMPROVEMENT-PLAN.md, which conflicts the same way
# and must keep doing so: union there would interleave two prose sections and
# silently accept two headings claiming the same section number.
scripts/skip-ledger.tsv merge=union
